  "name": "Speed and Offset",
  "kind": "video",
  "blurb": "A Julia set drifting on its own Speed, and its Offset to place it",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Everything that moves has a Timing heading, open here on the Julia Set, whose Time slides the rainbow round the set's orbits. Speed is how fast it runs, a multiple of its own pace: 2 is twice as fast, 0 holds it still and -1 runs it backwards. Offset is where it is in its cycle, 0 to 1. Set Speed to 0 and drag Offset to scrub through the whole drift by hand."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
